IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fk68-nouns`

-- Row il-68. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: three items (I1, I2, I3), each with its defect and a sound reference beside it as a control. Each recorded reference carries limb (a), limb (b) and how each was read.
-- Tests of the controls are in fk68-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings in fk68-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose are in fk68-tests-red.l4.
-- THE QUOTATION LINES. `src:N` lines are expanded by tools/srcquote.py from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (revision 2982012, UNOFFICIAL; N is the line of the whole page, listed in the excerpt's header),
-- so every claim resting only on them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY. `img:[instrument pPAGE]` lines give words printed on a deposited page image (a crop, named by instrument and printed page, in registers/source-bundle/);
-- they were read from the crop, checked word by word against the text layer of the PDF page (which stores the words in visual order) and read against the crop by eye. They are not expanded by a tool.
-- SH is Sefer HaChukim (the Knesset's laws); KT is Kovetz HaTakanot (regulations). Pages are printed pages.

§ `References`

-- ===== I1. Section 14(2) cites a subsection (a) of section 7; section 7 as the Knesset printed it in 1996 has no subsection letters =====
-- THE CITING WORDS, limb (b). SH 106 printed page 290, item 11, replaces section 14; paragraph (2) of the new section 14 reads:
